WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:06.700
For many years, one of the biggest criticisms
that I got from anybody, sales person that

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.980
worked for me was that I did not allow coffee
in our office.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:14.549
When I tell you no coffee, I still don't drink
coffee, I don't like coffee.

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:16.299
And everybody used to give me a hard time.

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:17.539
"Pat, how is it possible.

00:00:17.539 --> 00:00:18.539
You're OCD.

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:19.940
You do not like coffee.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.270
How does a sales office not have coffee?"

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.250
For me, it's many different reasons.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.430
One, I don't think we need coffee for energy.

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:30.020
I think our body needs to move for energy.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:31.020
But stains bother me.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.190
If I walk into a place with a stain, it bothers
me.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:37.280
I can't work in an environment with stains
all over the carpet.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:45.640
Well, years later, Mario, Alexis, Maral, and
many of the teammates came together, including

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.679
my wife, they came together and said, "We've
got to figure out a way to get Pat to have

00:00:49.679 --> 00:00:50.679
a coffee machine."

00:00:50.679 --> 00:00:54.410
So we had a coffee machine, and now that's
okay to have a coffee machine in the office.

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.390
But we added two other machines.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:05.071
I decided to add an 88 wine bottle dispenser
that looks like of like this.

00:01:05.071 --> 00:01:06.071
This is what it looks like.

00:01:06.071 --> 00:01:09.640
You literally can walk in, in the middle of
the day while you're working, have a glass

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.619
of wine, and go back to your desk and we're
okay with that.

00:01:12.619 --> 00:01:22.560
And Mario likes IPA beer and Tom likes Blue
Moon, so we also got a full on keg at the

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.509
office, with IPA and Blue Moon.

00:01:24.509 --> 00:01:28.100
So if you want to have a IPA and Blue Moon
in the middle of the day, or two, or three,

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:34.479
if your name is Tom and Mario, they'll be
some incredible strategy sessions.

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:37.200
Earlier today, where am I going with this?

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.909
I'm talking about what today?

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:40.670
How to Change Your Mood in 5 minutes.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:45.140
Because a glass of wine can change your mood
in five minutes, and provide better customer

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.140
service.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:51.820
Earlier today, we were having an ideation
session in our office and things got a little

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.200
out of hand.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:02:02.060
We saw a person, named Tom Ellsworth, that
probably shouldn't dance, was brave enough

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:09.009
to show us some of his incredible moves and
here's what it looked like.

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:12.459
[Tom dancing.]

00:02:12.459 --> 00:02:19.280
So, Tom, I just want to give a toast to you.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:27.340
May life be as rewarding as it was for us
while watching you perform that EPIC dance

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:30.780
move that I don't know many people can put
together.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:34.599
If we got Justin Timberlake, if we got Chris.

00:02:34.599 --> 00:02:40.099
. . if we got all of these guys together,
I don't know if they could put the moves together

00:02:40.099 --> 00:02:41.530
like you just did.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:45.860
You may have a career in choreography, but
I'm glad you're not choosing that route, and

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.160
you're going to be in business with us.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.390
So, toast to you.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.990
Now, with that being said, let me tell you
how you can change your mood, literally, in

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:52.990
five minutes.

00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:54.810
I've been doing this for the last 15 years.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:59.170
[I had to take a quick sip.]

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.819
So here's how simple it is.

00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:01.819
Listen.

00:03:01.819 --> 00:03:05.409
I will have, as a business owner, as an entrepreneur,
you go through a lot of different things.

00:03:05.409 --> 00:03:09.049
People hit you, you know you get this, you
get that, and you know, cancellations, this

00:03:09.049 --> 00:03:12.700
person, this employee's not happy, there's
an argument, there's a conflict, there's a

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:16.040
vendor issue, there's an attorney issue, there's
a lawsuit -- there's so many different things

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:17.860
that are going to hit you.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:18.860
Right?

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:22.640
And if you don't know how to snap out of it
quickly, your day is gone.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:23.989
And if your day is gone, your week is gone.

00:03:23.989 --> 00:03:26.120
And if your week is gone, your month is gone,
then you're out of business.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.260
So you've got to have a system.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.260
Everything's about systems.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:30.579
You've got to have a system.

00:03:30.579 --> 00:03:32.060
So how do you change your mood in 5 minutes?

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.299
There's a couple of things you can do.

00:03:33.299 --> 00:03:38.459
One of them is literally taking a walk, listen
to some music, the music that pumps you up,

00:03:38.459 --> 00:03:39.690
and come back up.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.489
Two is go do stairs.

00:03:41.489 --> 00:03:46.680
Go step, go do two or three floors yourself
and you'll snap out of it in no time because

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:50.700
your body is moving, blood is flowing through
your body.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:55.330
Three is literally watch a funny one-minute
video.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:04:00.040
Watch a funny one-minute video that makes
you laugh and you will completely be out of

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.040
that state.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.920
And four is my favorite system of all time.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:08.390
And by the way, there's probably hundreds
of ways of doing this, and there are many

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:09.390
great ones.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:12.659
I'm just giving you some basic ones that you
can implement today that can completely shift

00:04:12.659 --> 00:04:13.659
your attitude.

00:04:13.659 --> 00:04:15.360
Because the worst thing you can do is say,
"I'm going home."

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.592
That's what average people do, and they don't
make it.

00:04:16.592 --> 00:04:19.449
"Today was a bad day, I'm going to go home
early."

00:04:19.449 --> 00:04:20.449
Nope.

00:04:20.449 --> 00:04:21.449
You cannot do that.

00:04:21.449 --> 00:04:24.530
You will go out of business, your customers,
your team, your staff is depending on you

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.030
to show up even when you don't feel like it.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:31.170
And they're hoping that you're a leader and
you have a system to snap out of it, to help

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.170
you out in business.

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:33.170
You know, what my favorite one is?

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.170
Here's what my favorite one is.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:35.669
I've been using this for fifteen years.

00:04:35.669 --> 00:04:41.610
When I was in the Army, and we were in boot
camp, one time I'll never forget, this man

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:49.010
who was 29 years old, I was 18, he got a letter
from his ex, at the time it was his wife,

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:51.190
and it was a letter, I mean, this is in boot
camp.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.930
You can't call anybody.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:05:01.880
The letter said that I'm leaving you, and
I'm leaving you for a man that you know of

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:02.940
as well.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.669
And this guy wouldn't stop crying.

00:05:05.669 --> 00:05:06.919
He would not stop crying.

00:05:06.919 --> 00:05:09.940
He was so emotional, he was out of control.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:15.050
So one, I'm sitting there myself, and I'm
concerned because I haven't seen my friends

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:18.610
for awhile, all my friends miss me, all this,
all that, all these things that I'm thinking

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:24.300
about myself, my little problem that I have
and here I see somebody that's going through

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:27.490
what they're going through, the issues that
they're going through, and I'm sitting there

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:28.590
telling myself, you know what Pat?

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:29.590
Snap out of it.

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:35.490
No matter what situation you're in, I promise
you, there are millions if not billions of

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:41.069
people that would love to change their massive
problem that they have -- the loss of a loved

00:05:41.069 --> 00:05:47.660
one, you know, somebody completely breaking
their heart, losing everything, war, crime,

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:50.690
all this mess that they're going through,
there's a lot of people going through this.

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:53.330
They would love to exchange that with you.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:54.330
Many people.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:58.509
So #4 for me is to just kind of reflect and
sit there and say, listen, life is all good,

00:05:58.509 --> 00:06:02.870
